Found while working k213 on Windows 2026-11-22 (Windows 11 Pro 26H2, native run of a build of 1ea8353). The shipped demo config example/unreagent.yaml runs ping as the editor (args -n 999999 127.0.0.1) and sets no unreal.unattended, which defaults to true, so the launcher appends -unattended (cmd/launcher/lifecycle.go, the boolVal(u.Unattended) branch). ping rejects it ("invalid option -unattended"), exits 1 three times within 10 s, and the launcher gives up on the editor ("failed 3 times in a row ... giving up").

The release zip ships example/unreagent.yaml as the demo unreagent.yaml, so the first thing a new user runs gives up on its editor. Measured on Windows only; Linux ping would reject the option as well (unverified).

Fix candidate: unattended: false under unreal: in example/unreagent.yaml, with a comment why (the demo editor is not UnrealEditor). Owner: unreagent-worker (example/ in OWNERS); example/README.md (unreagent-doc-writer) if it describes the demo's output.

example/unreagent.yaml: unattended: false under unreal:, with a comment why (ping is not UnrealEditor and rejects -unattended; leave the key out for a real editor). TestExampleDemoConfigLoads (internal/config/load_test.go) already pinned the demo config; it now also pins unattended off and unreal.args — red without the yaml change, green with it. Full check green on Linux (gofmt, go vet, go test -count=1 ./..., make windows). NOT verified: the demo on Windows — nobody ran the fixed config there; unreal.unattended is read only in editorArgs (cmd/launcher/lifecycle.go), so ping now gets exactly -n 999999 127.0.0.1. On Linux ping still fails on the Windows arguments (exit 2 here), as example/README.md says. example/README.md (doc-writer): nothing in it becomes wrong; step 3 of 'Getting started' now holds on Windows. Optional for doc-writer: 'Switching to real' step 3 says remove unreal.editor/args — it should also name the new unattended: false line.

